{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Fighting the Competition", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Introducing the Competition ", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "scholar > Looking to the Stars > How Old is Old", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.1", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Comparatives", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " In English, it is common to describe things or people by talking about particular qualities or features that they have more of than someone or something. In order to do this, you need to use comparative adjectives. Adjectives are used to compare things.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "The comparative is used to compare two people, places, ideas or things.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When comparing two things that are equal, we use the form<span class=\"italic\"> as</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span> + <span class=\"italic\">as.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/><span class=\"italic\"> Our strategy is not as appealing as theirs.</span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When comparing two things that are different, we use the form <span class=\"italic\"> adjective</span> + <span class=\"italic\">-er than ...</span> or, for two or more syllable adjectives, <span class=\"italic\">more/less</span> + <span class=\"italic\">adjective</span> + <span class=\"italic\">than</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Examples:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">We have a stronger marketing record in Latin America than the competition. </span> <br/> <span class=\"italic\">Garcia Partners is more familiar with Latin American culture than Polygon.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Some adjectives have irregular comparative forms: good \u2192 better; bad \u2192 worse", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/> <span class=\"italic\"> We are better known and better established than the Garcia Partners.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes the comparison is implicit (you compare to something which is understood but not mentioned in the sentence).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"> We need to get a clearer picture of who we are dealing with.</span> ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Language for Asking and Giving Opinions ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": " In the business world, it is common to give your opinion about things. However, it is advisable to ask another person about their thoughts on something before you tell them how you feel about something. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": " Here are some ways in which you can ask and give opinions:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Asking for Opinions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Giving Opinions</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<ul><li>What do you know about \u2026 ? </li>\\t<li>What do you think of \u2026 ? </li><li>What do you think about \u2026 ? </li> <li>How d'you feel (about \u2026 )? </li> <li>\\tWhat d'you reckon (about \u2026 )? </li> <li>What's your opinion of \u2026 ? </li> <li>(What do think about) that? </li> <li>What are your views on \u2026 ? </li> <li>Where do you stand (on \u2026 )?</li></ul>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I believe \u2026<br/>  I reckon \u2026<br/> As far as I know, \u2026 <br/> If you ask me, \u2026<br/> Personally, ... <br/>To my mind, ... <br/> The way I see it, \u2026 <br/> To be honest/frank ...  <br/> To be honest/frank ...  \\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bid", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an offer to provide services for a specific price", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are going to be many companies trying to win this bid.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation at a PR agency. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "competition", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a situation in which organizations try to be more successful than other organizations", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're going to enter this competition to win.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "based in", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the place where you work or where your main business is", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are based in the States.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "e-commerce company", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a company which does its services  using a computer and the Internet", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They are an e-commerce company that provide sales services.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "web portal", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a website that helps you find other websites", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun):", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They do all their business via a web portal.  ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "business", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an organization that produces or sells goods or provides a service", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They also provide business-to-consumer sales. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get a foot in the door", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to have an opportunity ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They already work with that market while we still have to get a foot in the door. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to deal with", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do business with someone ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": " (verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We need to get a better understanding of who we're dealing with.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "consumer", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who buys and uses products and services", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They provide consumer-to-consumer sales. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn6le09ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Start the conversation with a greeting.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Tell him about a job related issue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask for your friend's opinion.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your dialogue with other people.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Change roles.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about jobs, work and technology.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I 